  "notes": [
    "Candidate. Never deployed. Dynamic quantization: weights are quantized ahead of time, activation scales are chosen at run time, so no calibration set was needed and none was used. This is not static PTQ and the record must not be read as one.",
    "The exporters refuse -int8 versions with 'INT8 export requires a calibration pass', which is true of static PTQ and not of this path. The refusal and these bytes are both correct; they are about different mechanisms - which is why mechanism is in the identity tuple and the word 'int8' alone is not enough to identify a release.",
    "precisionEvidence shows the mix a dynamically-quantized graph actually is: int8 weights alongside fp32 tensors the quantizer left behind. 'int8' is a majority, not a description of every tensor.",
    "The class list and both recommended thresholds are inherited from the fp32 sidecar. What that costs at 0.4 on these bytes is in parity.comparison.atRecommendedThreshold.",
    "Measured on macOS 26.6.2; the fp16 record's evidence was gathered on 26.5.1 (same architecture, same onnxruntime 1.29.0, same execution provider). The registry's target check is what surfaced that - the two candidates were not measured under identical conditions and their numbers should not be compared to each other as if they were.",
    "Stored under dist/, which is gitignored: verify will report MISSING on a fresh clone."
  ],
